      "summaries": {
        "en": "Skills is a repository of reusable, modular capabilities that enhance AI coding agents for .NET and C# development. It provides pre-built skills like code generation, testing, and debugging, enabling agents to perform complex tasks reliably. The project emphasizes composability, allowing developers to mix and match skills for custom workflows. Practically, you can integrate these skills into your AI agent to automate .NET project scaffolding, unit test creation, or code review. It's a practical toolkit for boosting AI-assisted .NET productivity.",
        "zh": "Skills 是一个面向 .NET 和 C# 开发的 AI 编码代理技能库，通过可复用模块化技能增强代理实用性。其核心将代码生成、测试、调试等常见任务封装为独立技能，支持按需组合调用，实现复杂工作流自动化。技术上强调组合性，开发者可像搭积木般自由搭配技能，定制专属开发助手。实际应用中，集成至 AI 代理后，可快速实现 .NET 项目脚手架搭建、单元测试自动生成或代码审查，是提升 AI 辅助 .NET 开发效率的开箱即用工具集。",
        "es": "Skills is a repository of reusable, modular capabilities that enhance AI coding agents for .NET and C# development. It provides pre-built skills like code generation, testing, and debugging, enabling agents to perform complex tasks reliably. The project emphasizes composability, allowing developers to mix and match skills for custom workflows. Practically, you can integrate these skills into your AI agent to automate .NET project scaffolding, unit test creation, or code review. It's a practical toolkit for boosting AI-assisted .NET productivity.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "skills stands out for agent-skills in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Skills is a repository of reusable, modular capabilities that enhance AI coding agents for .NET and C# development. It provides pre-built skills like code generation, testing, and debugging, enabling agents to perform complex tasks reliably. The project emphasizes composability, allowing developers to mix and match skills for custom workflows. Practically, you can integrate these skills into your AI agent to automate .NET project scaffolding, unit test creation, or code review. It's a practical toolkit for boosting AI-assisted .NET productivity.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/dotnet/skills for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
