      "summaries": {
        "en": "Forge is a Python framework for building self-hosted, multi-step agentic workflows with LLM tool-calling. Its key insight is a modular design that separates tool definitions, LLM backends (Ollama, llama.cpp, etc.), and workflow logic, enabling flexible composition. Use it to create custom AI agents that chain function calls, retrieve data, or automate tasks—all running locally for privacy and control.",
        "zh": "Forge是一个Python框架，用于构建自托管的多步骤智能体工作流，核心能力是让大语言模型调用工具并执行复杂任务。其技术亮点在于模块化设计：将工具定义、LLM后端（如Ollama、llama.cpp）和工作流逻辑解耦，开发者可灵活组合组件。例如，定义搜索和计算工具后，LLM能自动决定调用顺序。实际应用中，Forge适合构建本地AI助手，用于自动化数据检索、文档处理或代码生成，所有数据本地处理以保障隐私。用户可从单步工具调用逐步扩展为多步骤流程。",
        "es": "Forge is a Python framework for building self-hosted, multi-step agentic workflows with LLM tool-calling. Its key insight is a modular design that separates tool definitions, LLM backends (Ollama, llama.cpp, etc.), and workflow logic, enabling flexible composition. Use it to create custom AI agents that chain function calls, retrieve data, or automate tasks—all running locally for privacy and control.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "forge stands out for agentic-ai, agentic-workflow, and agents in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Forge is a Python framework for building self-hosted, multi-step agentic workflows with LLM tool-calling. Its key insight is a modular design that separates tool definitions, LLM backends (Ollama, llama.cpp, etc.), and workflow logic, enabling flexible composition. Use it to create custom AI agents that chain function calls, retrieve data, or automate tasks—all running locally for privacy and control.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/antoinezambelli/forge for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
